cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata. It is research software with no independent review: cite the version you ran, and read docs/RESULTS_AND_LIMITATIONS.md before relying on any number."
title: "ECONOSIM (PROMETHEUS-X): a research platform for computational economics, stochastic finance, and neural risk control"
type: software
version: 0.5.4
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Plovaxs/economisms"
url: "https://github.com/Plovaxs/economisms"
authors:
  - name: "PROMETHEUS maintainers"
abstract: >-
  ECONOSIM asks whether more model complexity earns its cost on quantitative economic and financial tasks.
  It compares classical, deep-learning and hybrid quantum models (neural SDEs, PDE solvers, multi-agent
  reinforcement learning, deep hedging, recession and inflation forecasting) against classical baselines, and
  publishes its negative and null results. Research and simulation only: not financial advice and not a
  live-trading system.
keywords:
  - computational economics
  - stochastic finance
  - neural SDE
  - deep hedging
  - reproducible research
  - negative results
